---
import Link from "../misc/Link.astro";
---

<section>
    <h3>
        Kova Builder
        <span class="title-aside"> 8 months, October 2024 to May 2025 </span>
    </h3>
    <p>
        <Link
            link="https://kova-builder.com/"
            name="KovaBuilder"
        /> is a company focused on building startups from scratch, aiming to niche cases in order to launch products that can be scalable and profitable in the future.
        Mostly of them are intermediaries between clients and users in the financial ambit, persuing an easy way for users to have a quick list of offers from the clients.
    </p>

    <p>
        I joined the company to be part of the new massification team, bringing the existing
        applications to new markets. We were in charge of the translations, adding the necessary content
        on the content manager and the precise language files on the applicaction itself. The tasks were useful to get an idea of how the applications worked in code level
        and see the prupose of each application. The applicataions were divided in two groups:
        <ul>
            <li>
                The monoliths ones: They were the applications that had front-end and back-end in the same project, using <Link
                link="https://www.codeigniter.com/"
                name="CodeIgniter4"/>. Those applications were the older ones they had.
            </li>
            <li>
                The not monoliths ones: They were the applications that had front-end and back-end separated in two different applications, using <Link
                link="https://www.codeigniter.com/"
                name="CodeIgniter4"/> as the back-end and <Link link="https://vuejs.org/" name="Vue" /> for the front-end.
                This was a new perspective of building the proyects that the company was using at the moment I joined.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </p>

    <p>
        As time passed, they moved me to a new team
        called "quick action team". There, we were assigned tasks daily that were
        mostly focused on the maintenance of the applications (taking care of bugs
        or unexpected behaviours), adding new APIs from clients to our applicataions or design changes.
        This was were I learned the most about the workflow the company used to mantain and make the applications.
        The tasks were full-stack ones, having the opportunity to learn about all the techs and external services the applications were using, such as <Link
            link="https://n8n.io/"
            name="N8N"
        /> or <Link
            link="https://www.bitrix24.es/"
            name="Bitrix24"
        />. 
    </p>

    <p>
        In the final part of my time with them, they assigned me tasks focused on the development of new
        functionalities and more complex maintenance tasks. Mostly of the maintenance tasks were back-end ones, as the Project Manager
        told me that I was good at tracing the problems to their root and analyzing the problems. But there were also front-end ones, focused
        on the new applications using the framework <Link link="https://vuejs.org/" name="Vue" />. 
    </p>

    <p>
        As a summary, here are some things I did as part of their team:
        <ul>
            <li>
                Massification of applications, bringing the applications to other markets applying translations and new APIs.
            </li>
            <li>
                Maintenance and fixes of the applications (including their own CM and CRM ones), entering the full-stack team.
            </li>
            <li>
                Developing new functionalities to the applications.
            </li>
            <li>
                Maintenance and fixes of more complicated and complex tasks on the back-end part.
            </li>
            <li>
                Developing a completely new functionality of the application in the front-end part, pairing with the back-end developer of the application.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </p>
</section>

<style>
    section {
        max-width: 55rem;
        margin-bottom: 5rem;
    }

    h3 {
        border-bottom: 1px dashed #00000020;
    }

    h3:not(:nth-child(-n + 2)) {
        margin-top: 3rem;
    }

    .title-aside {
        float: right;
    }

    li {
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
</style>
